; nqueens.n — N-queens by iterative backtracking (bench/SPEC.md)
; N from argv[1] (default 11). Explicit-stack search: cols[r] = placed column
; of row r, nxt[r] = next column to try. (r, c) conflicts with row i when
; cols[i]==c or |cols[i]-c|==|r-i| (two signed tests — no abs needed).
11 n!
has_args 'setn if
n@ int array cols!
n@ 1 add int array nxt!
0 cnt!
nxt@ 0 0 set
0 d!
'oc 'ob while
"solutions: " print cnt@ print
ret
setn: 1 arg_index n! ret
oc: d@ 0 gte ret
ob:
  nxt@ d@ get c!
  0 found!
  'ac 'ab while
  c@ n@ lt 'place 'back if_else
  ret
ac: found@ not c@ n@ lt and ret
ab:
  0 i! 1 sf!
  'sc 'sb while
  sf@ 'found1 'nextc if_else
  ret
sc: i@ d@ lt sf@ and ret
sb:
  cols@ i@ get ci!
  ci@ c@ eq
  ci@ c@ sub i@ d@ sub eq
  ci@ c@ sub i@ d@ sub add 0 eq
  or or bad!
  sf@ bad@ not and sf!
  i++
  ret
found1: 1 found! ret
nextc: c++ ret
place:
  cols@ d@ c@ set
  nxt@ d@ c@ 1 add set
  d++
  nxt@ d@ 0 set
  d@ n@ eq 'full if
  ret
full: cnt++ d@ 1 sub d! ret
back: d@ 1 sub d! ret
